# L §7.3 The error bound: "A printed result that rests on rounded transcendentals, with no round after them, prints
# ≈ and a bound".  pdf(d, k) to 1e-30 is a correctly rounded transcendental; a mean over keys of it (L §5.11 queries
# over keys), the weights normalised by their sum, and their sum all rest on it: each prints ≈ (only the ≈ is checked
# here; its digits are the interpreter's).
=== m.tally
model p13
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-18
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "synthetic"

index ks = int 1..3

input mu: num
input sd: num

def d: dist = normal(mu, sd) to 1e-6
def p[k in ks]: num = pdf(d, k) to 1e-30
def w[k in ks]: num = p[k] / sum(p[j] for j in ks)

ask q1: mean(p[k] for k in ks) orient higher
ask q2: w[1] orient higher
ask q3: mean(w[k] for k in ks) orient higher

version v1
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  mu = 2
  sd = 1
=== expect
q1: ≈ ...
  cut 2026-10-18
  orient higher
q2: ≈ ...
  cut 2026-10-18
  orient higher
q3: ≈ ...
  cut 2026-10-18
  orient higher
